  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlife Crime Prevention (WCP) Alinea, 2023-2026 - Wildlife Crime Prevention (WCP) Combatting Illegal Wildlife Trade</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Wildlife Crime Prevention (WCP) Alinea, 2023-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the intervention is to to strengthen counter wildlife crime (CWC) work at the regional level, in areas of significant biodiversity, by supporting organizations working on the entire chain of law enforcement, including prevention, response, investigations, legal processes and public awareness. 

On a long term perspective, the expected impact of the intervention is to create safer communities adjacent to significant areas of significant biodiversity through effective and deliberate law enforcement interventions against wildlife crime and IWT syndicates who capitalize on exploiting vulnerable people.
The overarching objective of this proposal is to create safer communities adjacent to significant areas of biodiversity through effective and deliberate law enforcement interventions on IWT syndicates who capitalise on exploiting vulnerable people. This objective will be implemented with partners under the Alinea Pillars of Support-Connect-Promote in three critical landscapes in Southern Africa.
The identified landscapes in which partners will be supported under this proposal are:
1. The Greater Kruger Landscape  based around the border region of South Africa, Mozambique, and Zimbabwe.
2. The Zambezi Landscape  based around the border regions of Zambia, Angola, Namibia, Botswana, and Zimbabwe.
3. The Democratic Republic of Congo  based around key transnational IWT trafficking hotspots in the DRC.
The intervention has three main work streams:
1. Support - aims to facilitate the means for WCP to provide support to regional partners in line with the Alinea strategic lines of work and to facilitate administrative capabilities of regional partners. 
2. Connect - support collaboration and unification of efforts through the development of working and knowledge platforms with the regional partners and support key interventions across identified landscapes.  
3. Promote - develop the capacity of Alinea partners to counter IWT, promote the safeguarding of human rights and promote and develop social impact in programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WCP is a not-for-profit organisation established in 2016 with the goal of capacitating partners, both government and other conservation institutions, where there are key gaps and need for collaboration in protecting wildlife and wild areas. WCP was built around five pillars: Law Enforcement, Wildlife Criminal Justice, Awareness, Strategic Intelligence and Regional Collaboration. To share its experience, and since illegal wildlife trade is a cross-border business, WCP established a regional cooperation programme called Alinea. Alinea&apos;s overall goal is to create safer communities in districts bordering areas of significant biodiversity, through effective and targeted law enforcement interventions against illegal wildlife trade syndicates that exploit vulnerable people. Within Alinea, WCP supports non-governmental organisations working on similar issues in southern, east and central Africa,to increase their operational and administrative capacity, and promote networking and collaboration.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">WCP &#xe4;r en enskild organisation som etablerades 2016 f&#xf6;r att bygga kapacitet hos myndigheter och andra naturv&#xe5;rdsinstitutioner. Verksamheten utf&#xf6;rs inom fem pelare: brottsbek&#xe4;mpning, viltbrottstraffr&#xe4;tt, information, strategisk underr&#xe4;ttelseinformation och regionalt samarbete. F&#xf6;r att dela med sig av sin erfarenhet, och d&#xe5; illegal handel med vilda djur &#xe4;r en gr&#xe4;ns&#xf6;verskridande verksamhet, s&#xe5; etablerade WCP ett regionalt samarbetsprogram som kallas f&#xf6;r Alinea. Inom Alinea st&#xf6;djer WCP enskilda organisationer som arbetar med liknande fr&#xe5;gor i s&#xf6;dra, centrala och &#xf6;stra Afrika. Alineas &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att skapa s&#xe4;krare samh&#xe4;llen i distrikt som gr&#xe4;nsar till omr&#xe5;den med betydande biologisk m&#xe5;ngfald, genom effektiva och avsiktliga brottsbek&#xe4;mpande ingripanden mot syndikat f&#xf6;r illegal handel med vilda djur och v&#xe4;xter som utnyttjar utsatta m&#xe4;nniskor. Mer specifikt syftar Alinea till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra operationell och administrativ kapacitet hos organisationerna, samt fr&#xe4;mja n&#xe4;tverkande och samarbete.</narrative>
  </description>
